    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d642">

                <pb facs="0742" n="726" xml:id="pg726"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/3–2747</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Charles C. Hauch of the Division of Caribbean
                        Affairs, to the Haitian Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Charles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-27">March 27, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I am enclosing two copies
                    of the Department’s press release of last night setting forth the exchange of
                    correspondence with the Haitian Good Will Mission.<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d642-f1"/> As you are aware, release of this correspondence was
                    suggested by the Haitian Government to the American Embassy at Port-au-Prince
                    and this Government was pleased to give publicity to these documents
                    simultaneously with their release in Haiti.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles</hi> C. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Hauch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d642-f1" n="18" xml:id="d642-f1-content">
                <p>The press release consisted of a statement by the Department, printed in
                    Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, April 6, 1947, p.
                    634, together with the exchange of correspondence comprising 26 pages of notes
                    and memoranda. The correspondence was issued in mimeographed form but was not
                    printed. Two of the Department’s notes, dated March 17, are printed <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg720">pp. 720</ref> and <ref
                        target="#pg723">723</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
